Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:58:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/53] B70-V6x: riceharvest gdn_mixed_no_sync (default off,
 B70_GDN_MIXED_NO_SYNC)

riceharvest/vllm b70/v0.32 4cc29dd3ef patch_gdn_mixed_no_sync: in a mixed
step (spec decodes + prefills), GDNAttentionMetadataBuilder.build() builds
the spec / non-spec row indices and both query_start_loc cumsums on the host
and sends them in one async H2D copy, instead of six host-mask gathers of
device tensors (each a blocking index copy). The row indices travel in the
metadata (b70_spec_rows / b70_non_spec_rows), so update_block_table() for
the other GDN KV-cache groups gathers with them too. Same values.

Hand-merged with #64479 (already in this trunk: supports_update_block_table
on XPU, the xpu seq_lens assert in mamba_utils): the cherry-pick applies
clean on top, and with #64479 the update_block_table() branch is the one the
XPU path takes for the extra groups.

B70-V6x change: rice's gate defaults on ("1", off with =0). Here it is
opt-in, B70_GDN_MIXED_NO_SYNC=1; unset, build() and update_block_table() run
the stock mask gathers (b70_* rows stay None). The cookbook marks it "not
yet GPU-tested"; not GPU-tested here either.

Generated from patches/b70/patch_gdn_mixed_no_sync.py of
riceharvest/b70-qwen38-cookbook@9f7fa83.
